This repository is a Derivative Work: a Core ML conversion of Liquid-Codec for Apple Silicon.
- models/lc_dec_ane_int8.mlmodelc, models/lc_dec_ane.mlmodelc, models/lc_tail_f32.bin: Liquid AI's decoder weights, converted (int8 and fp16 Core ML programs; float32 tail). Fixed 40-frame window from the original conversion.
- models/stream/: the same decoder weights re-converted for 1, 2, and 4 new frames (ctx=20), plus the encoder weights as a one-frame Core ML step with a key/value cache (fp16, and int8 on the LFM stack only). Produced by convert/build_models.py.
- models/liquidcodec.json: manifest for the streaming packages (tensor names, cache length, latency).
- convert/lc_ane.py: modified re-implementation of Liquid AI's decoder modeling code (changes listed at the top of the file). Parameterized chunk length.
- convert/lc_enc.py, convert/lc_step.py: modified re-implementation of Liquid AI's encoder (STFT front end, full-causal LFM, finite-scalar quantizer) in the same ANE layout. Changes are listed at the top of each file.
- convert/build_models.py, convert/export_tail.py, examples/: new code. The Swift example now streams encode and decode.
